# Miner Llama v5 preset: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, Unsloth's UD-Q5_K_S (with the MTP layer) on four GTX 1070 8 GB cards,
# 131,072-token context, the MTP head as the pipeline's guesser.
# Build: the fork's branch pascal-p106-v5 with PRs #3-#7 merged (2026-11-20; until a v5 release). Measured on
# Windows 10 with a CUDA 12.9 sm_61 build; the switches are not Windows-specific, but this line has not been run on
# Linux. README.md has the numbers and what each switch is worth;
# two speeds for one setting are the contributor's slowest and fastest runs.
# What each line does to the replies: the tag at the start of its comment (docs/reply_effects.md; python3 -I
# scripts/preset_effects.py counts them). Here 1 [mode] (reasoning off), 2 [order], 4 [draft], 7 [same]; no sampling
# values are set, so the server's defaults apply unless the client sends its own.
# Use: . settings.env && env $PRESET_ENV llama-server -m "$MODELS/$PRESET_MODEL" $PRESET_ARGS --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
PRESET_MODEL=Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q5_K_S.gguf

PRESET_ENV=
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_DRAFT_SHORTLIST=65536"  # [draft] the MTP head scores token ids below 65,536 plus special and context tokens: the guesser 50.4 tok/s instead of 29.4, the same hit rate (PR #6)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_HOP_MAILBOX=1 GGML_CUDA_HOP_MAILBOX_TIMEOUT_MS=1000"  # [same] the polling mailbox for small card-to-card hops
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_HOP_MAILBOX_MAX_KB=0 GGML_CUDA_HOP_MAILBOX_GATE_KB=64"  # [same] hops above 64 KiB through pinned buffers ordered by events, nothing polls or times out: a 39.5k prompt reads at 572 and 591 tok/s instead of 281 and 289, and a 125k prompt passes (PR #4). Without GATE_KB, MAX_KB=0 is the uncapped mailbox that timed out on long prompts
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_PIPE_GRAMMAR=1"  # [draft] the pipe's guesses are still checked by the model under the grammar; the pipe keeps running under a grammar (tool calls, JSON schemas): a 39.5k tool call writes at 53.1 and 55.6 tok/s instead of 31.5 and 32.1 (PR #7)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_ARG_CTX_CHECKPOINTS_VRAM=2"  # [same] the slot's newest two checkpoints of the recurrent state on the cards
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_GRAPHS_FORCE=1 LLAMA_SERVER_YIELD=2 LLAMA_SAMPLING_TOP_K_ROWS=1 LLAMA_KV_SEQ_RM_BOUND=1"  # [same] v4's generic switches, as on the other presets
PRESET_ENV=${PRESET_ENV# }

PRESET_ARGS="--alias qwen36 -ngl 99 -c 131072 -np 1 --load-mode none -fa on --jinja --reasoning off"  # [mode] the run line: --reasoning off, so the model answers without thinking first; no sampling values are set, so the server's defaults apply unless the client sends its own; -fa on sets the arithmetic's order
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS -ctk f16 -ctv f16"  # [same] f16 cache: on Pascal the stock q8_0 decode attention is slower (tool-call writing +34 % at 39k with f16), and 131k fits in f16
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS -ts 0.85/1/1.05/1.1 -ub 128"  # [order] the micro-batch size sets the arithmetic's order; layers weighted off GPU 0, which also holds the MTP layer; -ub 128 reads long prompts ~5 % faster than 256 and frees ~330 MB on GPU 0
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --spec-type draft-mtp -ctkd q8_0 -ctvd q8_0 --spec-draft-backend-sampling"  # [draft] the draft's cache in Q8_0 touches only its guesses; the model's own MTP layer as the draft, its cache in q8_0
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS -bs --pipe-depth 2 --pipe-guess mtp --pipe-mtp-walk 1000"  # [draft] -bs samples on the cards (the same distribution, other draws); pipelined speculation with the MTP head as the guesser: 1,290 right / 208 wrong per 1,500 tokens against 458 / 585 for cont (PR #7)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --mtp-device 0"  # [same] the MTP layer and a copy of the output head (515 MiB) on GPU 0: on the last card a row waited behind pipe work under Windows' WDDM, 15.5 tok/s against 38 and 40 (PR #7)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --spec-ckpt-vram --ctx-checkpoints-incall"  # [order] keeps a prompt's call whole, so its micro-batches differ from a cut call's; the per-step speculation checkpoint (62.8 MiB) kept on the card instead of crossing the x1 link: a 49-token JSON answer 1.5 and 1.7 s instead of 3.9 (PR #5)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --cache-ram 3072"  # [same] cross-conversation prompt cache in host memory (8 GB host)
